# Build context hygiene. Two reasons, in order of importance:
#   1. .env must never reach an image layer — layers are shipped, .env is not.
#   2. Copying node_modules/.next from the host would shadow what the image
#      builds and silently ship a stale or wrong-platform artifact.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
!.env.example

node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist
.next
**/.next
out
**/out
coverage
**/coverage
.turbo
**/.turbo
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

.git
.github
docs
uploads
tmp
*.log
.DS_Store
.idea
.vscode
